1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:04,290
For years, Scribd was called
“the Netflix of books”.

2
00:00:04,440 --> 00:00:06,200
Today it's called Everand…

3
00:00:06,240 --> 00:00:09,360
and with its cheapest plan,
you pick one book a month.

4
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:10,610
Yes: one.

5
00:00:10,840 --> 00:00:11,890
What happened?

6
00:00:12,040 --> 00:00:13,860
And is it still worth it?

7
00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:18,500
We analyzed it in depth, with all
the data and sources on our blog:

8
00:00:18,540 --> 00:00:20,280
link in the description.

9
00:00:20,320 --> 00:00:25,160
Everand was born in 2023,
when Scribd split in two:

10
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:27,400
Scribd kept the documents,

11
00:00:27,440 --> 00:00:31,600
and Everand got the ebooks,
audiobooks and podcasts.

12
00:00:31,640 --> 00:00:35,240
And since 2025, they're
paid for separately.

13
00:00:35,280 --> 00:00:38,840
In October 2024,
“unlimited” came to an end.

14
00:00:38,880 --> 00:00:43,640
Now it works with unlocks: the Standard
plan gives you one book a month;

15
00:00:43,680 --> 00:00:46,893
Plus, three; and Deluxe, five.

16
00:00:46,933 --> 00:00:48,960
Which books need an unlock?

17
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:51,720
The official answer: “most of them”.

18
00:00:51,760 --> 00:00:55,480
Without unlocking, you get
about 20,000 rotating titles,

19
00:00:55,520 --> 00:00:57,000
out of 1.5 million.

20
00:00:57,040 --> 00:00:59,827
Unused unlocks are kept
for up to 6 months…

21
00:00:59,867 --> 00:01:02,360
but if you cancel, you lose the books:

22
00:01:02,400 --> 00:01:04,740
it's a rental, not a purchase.

23
00:01:04,780 --> 00:01:06,100
How much does it cost?

24
00:01:06,140 --> 00:01:11,060
In Spain, Plus costs €14.99 a month:

25
00:01:11,100 --> 00:01:12,980
about €5 per book.

26
00:01:13,020 --> 00:01:16,660
In Mexico, Standard costs 149 pesos.

27
00:01:16,700 --> 00:01:21,140
And in the US, the most expensive
plan costs more per book than Plus,

28
00:01:21,180 --> 00:01:22,600
according to its own website.

29
00:01:22,640 --> 00:01:23,880
What about Spanish?

30
00:01:23,920 --> 00:01:26,680
We estimate about 41,000 audiobooks,

31
00:01:26,720 --> 00:01:29,080
with Penguin Random House and Planeta:

32
00:01:29,120 --> 00:01:32,240
García Márquez, Vargas Llosa, Ruiz Zafón,

33
00:01:32,280 --> 00:01:34,410
Pérez-Reverte, Posteguillo…

34
00:01:34,560 --> 00:01:36,680
But they all require an unlock.

35
00:01:36,720 --> 00:01:39,800
Only about 600 in Spanish
come without limits,

36
00:01:39,840 --> 00:01:41,400
like “Crime and Punishment”…

37
00:01:41,440 --> 00:01:43,050
abridged to 2 hours.

38
00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:47,610
And some use a synthetic voice:
check the narrator before unlocking.

39
00:01:47,660 --> 00:01:51,460
The app, though, is very
polished: downloads,

40
00:01:51,500 --> 00:01:54,740
speed, sleep timer,
and it works on the web,

41
00:01:54,780 --> 00:01:57,660
on mobile, CarPlay and Android Auto.

42
00:01:57,700 --> 00:02:00,740
What's missing:
profiles and a family plan.

43
00:02:00,780 --> 00:02:04,900
Careful with the free trial:
30 days if you sign up on the web,

44
00:02:04,940 --> 00:02:08,020
but only 7 in the app,
and with just one book,

45
00:02:08,060 --> 00:02:09,980
whichever plan you choose.

46
00:02:10,020 --> 00:02:12,300
It asks for a card and
renews automatically.

47
00:02:12,340 --> 00:02:14,260
And if you subscribed from your phone,

48
00:02:14,300 --> 00:02:18,700
you cancel through Apple or Google,
where it may show up as “Scribd”.

49
00:02:18,740 --> 00:02:23,860
Reviews reflect this: on Google
Play it has a 4.4 in Spain,

50
00:02:23,900 --> 00:02:26,567
but a 3.5 in the US,

51
00:02:26,607 --> 00:02:29,980
where complaints almost
quadrupled after the change.

52
00:02:30,020 --> 00:02:33,900
And in September, Scribd
reported a security incident:

53
00:02:33,940 --> 00:02:36,740
if you have an account,
change your password.

54
00:02:36,780 --> 00:02:39,940
The best: a huge catalog in Spanish,

55
00:02:39,980 --> 00:02:43,860
with new releases, plus ebooks
and audiobooks in the same app.

56
00:02:43,900 --> 00:02:46,420
The worst: it's no longer unlimited,

57
00:02:46,460 --> 00:02:50,380
the books aren't yours,
and the trial has fine print.

58
00:02:50,420 --> 00:02:51,740
Who is it for?

59
00:02:51,780 --> 00:02:55,260
If you listen to one or two books
a month and want new releases,

60
00:02:55,300 --> 00:02:57,207
Plus can be worth it.

61
00:02:57,247 --> 00:02:58,380
If you listen to more,

62
00:02:58,420 --> 00:03:03,633
Audible offers unlimited listening
to its catalog for €9.99,

63
00:03:03,673 --> 00:03:07,260
and Storytel for €8.99.

64
00:03:07,300 --> 00:03:09,820
And for free classics, you already know:

65
00:03:09,860 --> 00:03:11,260
El Libro Total.

66
00:03:11,300 --> 00:03:12,300
The catch?

67
00:03:12,340 --> 00:03:16,380
It's no longer unlimited, even
though many people still think it is.

68
00:03:16,420 --> 00:03:19,540
Our score: 6.2 out of 10.

69
00:03:19,580 --> 00:03:22,900
And to find out where each
audiobook is cheapest for you,

70
00:03:22,940 --> 00:03:24,780
search for it on SonorBooks.

71
00:03:24,820 --> 00:03:27,470
Your next story is waiting for you.
